Subject: Cantor Inference Frame Staging and Reentry

Description: The anticipatory pre-inference stages, readiness gate, late-discovery classifier, and clean reentry rules that load materially required SOP before consequential inference while preserving bounded demand unfolding.

& [InferenceFrameManifest] is the immutable description of one prepared inference frame
  + [frame_uuid] is stable frame identity
  + [input_snapshot] is the exact user or job input
  + [subject_binding] is the focused semantic identity and known aliases
  + [purpose_binding] is the intended result and non-goals
  + [consequence_class] is the harm, authority, cost, reversibility, and uncertainty profile
  + [term_binding_set] is resolved material terms and contextual anchors
  + [dependency_closure] is the signed SOP definitions, contracts, operations, faculties, schemas, and policies required before inference
  + [artifact_set] is digest-bound source and reference material admitted to the frame
  + [faculty_set] is required and conditionally available FacultyPrograms
  + [query_trigger_set] is unresolved semantic conditions that must cause demand loading
  + [exclusion_set] is deliberately omitted material with criterion and justification
  + [unknown_set] is material limits that remain unresolved
  + [budget] is token, retrieval, traversal, inference, review, time, and effect limits
  + [frame_digest] is the immutable identity of all authoritative frame inputs
  = must: distinguish authoritative dependencies from optional background
  = must: remain compact through semantic addresses and verified projections rather than copying every source in full

& [AnticipatoryInferenceStaging] is the pre-inference preparation pipeline
  + [stage_1_capture] is freeze the exact input, caller, requested result, and conversation or job state
  + [stage_2_orient] is bind subject, purpose, non-goals, consequence, authority, and current-state claims
  + [stage_3_scan] is extract material terms, ambiguities, entities, actions, effects, claims, and likely faculty pressures
  + [stage_4_resolve] is query Cantor for signed definitions, governing contracts, operations, policies, and source artifacts
  + [stage_5_close] is traverse declared required dependencies until closure, bounded stop, or unresolved fault
  + [stage_6_challenge] is seek counterevidence, conflicting authority, excluded perspectives, dangerous assumptions, and anti-enchantment faults
  + [stage_7_compose] is build the minimum materially sufficient InferenceFrameManifest and faculty plan
  + [stage_8_readiness] is apply the FrameReadinessGate
  + [stage_9_infer] is invoke the provider only after readiness or an explicitly bounded exploratory exception
  + [stage_10_checkpoint] is validate the return and classify every newly requested or discovered dependency
  + [stage_11_review] is freeze the result in an InferenceCapsule and determine accept, revise, reframe, reset, query, yield, or stop
  = must: perform retrieval planning without adopting a substantive conclusion before frame readiness
  = must: scale staging depth with consequence and semantic novelty
  - never: use preflight anticipation as a claim that later retrieval will be unnecessary

& [AnticipatoryDependencyResolver] is the bounded prediction of required SOP and artifacts
  + [deterministic_inputs] is explicit terms, file references, operation names, effect types, contracts, and declared dependencies
  + [graph_inputs] is semantic neighbors, required edges, faculty activation predicates, and policy closure
  + [model_assistance] is optional non-authoritative classification of implicit topics, ambiguities, missing perspectives, and likely dependencies
  + [closure_rule] is follow every required dependency edge until resolved, rejected, deferred with reason, cyclic, or budget-bounded
  + [sufficiency_rule] is all root meanings, governing contracts, hard gates, required faculties, effect policies, and material evidence classes are bound
  = must: validate model-proposed dependencies through Cantor before admission
  = must: record unresolved dependencies and their consequence
  - never: let correlation weight alone make an artifact authoritative

& [FrameReadinessGate] is the decision to permit substantive inference
  + [ready] is material identity, purpose, authority, governing SOP, evidence classes, required faculties, and hard constraints are sufficiently bound
  + [ready_with_declared_limits] is unresolved items are explicit and do not prevent an honest bounded result
  + [exploratory_only] is inference may ask questions or propose retrieval but may not form a consequential conclusion
  + [not_ready] is a material term, authority, gate, artifact, contradiction, or required perspective remains unbound
  = must: block consequential inference while not_ready
  = must: include the frame digest in every provider call and return
  = must: make the readiness reason inspectable

& [LateDiscovery] is an artifact, dependency, condition, or meaning found after inference begins
  + [discovery_anchor] is its source, digest, retrieval cause, and discovery checkpoint
  + [affected_set] is prior bindings, premises, faculty selections, gates, conclusions, and effects that it may change
  + [materiality] is whether a reasonable compliant inference could differ after admitting it
  + [authority_impact] is whether purpose, principal, permission, policy, or governing SOP changes
  + [frame_delta_digest] is the identity difference between the old and proposed frame
  = must: classify the discovery before using it to continue inference
  = must: suspend effects until its impact is resolved

| [FrameChangeClass] is (append_safe | reframe_required | capsule_reset)

& [AppendSafeChange] is a non-material extension
  + [criterion] is the discovery adds detail without changing authority, semantic identity, polarity, hard gates, required faculties, material evidence balance, or any adopted premise
  + [transition] is append the verified artifact, update the frame digest, perform local validation, and continue from the checkpoint
  = must: preserve the old and new digest relationship
  - never: classify contradictory or conclusion-changing evidence as append_safe

& [ReframeRequiredChange] is a material change within the same job identity
  + [criterion] is the discovery changes a material definition, premise, evidence balance, counterevidence, faculty need, constraint, or inference path while subject, purpose, principal, and root authority remain stable
  + [transition] is freeze the current candidate as superseded, rebuild the frame, and rerun inference from the last clean pre-inference checkpoint
  + [anchoring_control] is the clean rerun receives the immutable input and corrected frame, not the invalidated reasoning text
  + [comparison] is a later review may compare old and new capsules without making the old candidate authoritative
  = must: explain which prior propositions were invalidated or require reconsideration

& [CapsuleResetChange] is a foundational identity or authority change
  + [criterion] is subject identity, root purpose, principal, authority grant, governing policy, signed package, consequence class, or foundational input changes enough to define a different inference event
  + [transition] is close the prior capsule with reset lineage and start a fresh capsule, frame, and provider context
  = must: carry source history and unresolved facts as provenance
  = must: avoid carrying invalidated conclusions as active context
  - never: silently continue under the old frame digest

& [MidInferenceQueryBoundary] is safe demand unfolding after readiness
  + [allowed_query] is an unanticipated term, subject criterion, operation dependency, contradiction, or review fault triggers sop_query
  + [provider_behavior] is the current generation yields or emits a tool request and continuation occurs in a new checkpointed provider call
  + [admission] is Cantor verifies the returned bundle and applies FrameChangeClass
  + [continuation] is append, reframe, or reset according to materiality rather than provider preference
  = must: preserve the complete query, bundle, frame-delta, and continuation chain
  - never: let the model absorb a material late artifact and continue as though its earlier reasoning were unaffected

& [DriftAndHallucinationControls] is the frame-integrity policy
  + [digest_binding] is every call is bound to exact input, frame, faculty, and dependency digests
  + [premise_ledger] is material conclusions cite the bindings and evidence on which they depend
  + [uncertainty_carry] is unresolved uncertainty survives every continuation
  + [context_freshness] is material reframing uses a clean provider pass
  + [candidate_isolation] is invalidated reasoning is retained for audit but excluded from the clean active frame
  + [review] is a separate capsule review checks missed dependencies, unsupported claims, frame drift, and incorrect change classification
  = must: prefer an explicit reset over preserving conversational momentum when foundational meaning changes
  - never: treat a fresh context as sufficient without correcting the frame that caused the fault

& [RequirementSet] is the traceable inference-staging collection
  + [CFS-001] is create an immutable InferenceFrameManifest before substantive inference
  + [CFS-002] is anticipate material SOP and artifact dependencies through deterministic, graph, and bounded model-assisted resolution
  + [CFS-003] is require a consequence-sensitive FrameReadinessGate
  + [CFS-004] is retain demand unfolding for genuinely unanticipated dependencies
  + [CFS-005] is classify late discoveries as append_safe, reframe_required, or capsule_reset
  + [CFS-006] is rerun material frame changes from a clean checkpoint without invalidated reasoning as active context
  + [CFS-007] is reset the capsule when subject, purpose, principal, authority, policy, package, or foundational input changes
  + [CFS-008] is bind calls and continuations to frame digests and preserve complete lineage
  + [CFS-009] is review missed dependencies, hallucination, drift, and incorrect materiality classification

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the inference-staging justification record
  + [fold_1_subject] is anticipating SOP attention-language and artifact needs before consequential inference
  + [fold_2_boundary] is minimum material dependency readiness inside; impossible total foresight and whole-library loading outside
  + [fold_3_data_design] is frame manifest, dependency closure, readiness, late discovery, materiality, frame delta, checkpoint, capsule, and reset lineage
  + [fold_4_governance] is consequence-scaled staging, signed admission, effects suspension, digest binding, clean reframing, and anti-enchantment review
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is capture, orient, scan, resolve, close, challenge, compose, gate, infer, checkpoint, and review
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is premature inference, missed dependency, false closure, late anchoring, silent frame mutation, reset avoidance, and invalidated-reasoning carryover
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is staging architecture formed while implementation remains within the existing bounded query-microkernel and capsule proof sequence

& [CantorInferenceFrameStagingSatisfactionSignature] is the valid SJS processing signature
  + [signature_protocol_uuid] is ad10f10f-d506-48ef-a805-f8b0a133766c
